    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "so the burning is just the acidity? i always thought it was like some kind of waste building up that's just clogging things up. is it like a sudden buildup of junk in the system?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That's a very common misconception! The burning isn't from \"junk\" clogging your muscles—it's specifically the hydrogen ions (the \"acid\" part of lactic acid) lowering the pH in your muscle cells. That acidity directly stimulates pain receptors, creating that intense burn.\n\nInstead of being a waste product, lactic acid is actually a rapid fuel source that your fast-twitch fibers use to keep contracting under stress. Your body clears it quickly after exercise by shuttling it to the liver and heart, where it's repurposed for energy, so there's no lingering \"clogging\" after you finish.",
      "source": "target",
